## Control {{controlId}}: Protect System Media Containing CUI, Both Paper and Digital

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization protects system media containing CUI within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through BitLocker encryption, sensitivity labels, and application protection policies managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if bitLockerEnforced}}
**Digital Media Encryption:**
BitLocker Drive Encryption protects CUI at rest on {{deviceCount}} managed endpoints, ensuring data confidentiality on physical media even in cases of device loss or theft.
{{/if}}

{{#if dlpLabelsConfigured}}
**Sensitivity Label Protection:**
{{dlpLabelsCount}} sensitivity labels enforce automated protection on digital media:
{{#each labels}}
- **{{name}}**{{#if isActive}} (Active){{else}} (Inactive){{/if}} — Priority: {{priority}}
{{/each}}

Labels apply encryption, access restrictions, and visual markings to documents stored on digital media across M365 workloads.
{{else}}
Sensitivity labels have not been configured for digital media protection.
{{/if}}

{{#if appProtectionsActive}}
**Mobile Media Protection:**
{{appProtectionsCount}} application protection policies prevent CUI from being saved to unprotected media locations:
{{#if policies}}
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{platformType}}) — {{#if isAssigned}}Assigned{{else}}Not Assigned{{/if}} — Protection: {{protectionLevel}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

**Paper Media:** CUI in paper form is stored in locked containers in controlled access areas. Paper media handling follows procedures documented in "Media Protection Policy v1.0."

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine BitLocker deployment reports, sensitivity label configurations, application protection policies, and paper media storage procedures.

